b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ HARNESS POSING incremental;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ PROVENANCE author: implementation-algol-60, an agent (Claude Opus 5.5, claude-opus-5-5);
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ PROVENANCE precursor seen: no;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ PROVENANCE idioms: the Revised Report on ALGOL 60 (1962) for blocks, procedures with value and name parameters (4.7, 5.4), the for statement with a while element (4.6) and conditional statements and expressions (3.3, 4.5), the name parameters letting one evaluator of an equation serve both equations (4.7.3.2), the X1 system's input and output procedures read, print, PRINTTEXT and NLCR, as the harness README gives them (harnesses/algol-60/README.md, 2.1) and its own X1 programs cite them (Kruseman Aretz 2003, chapter 7), and the X1 compiler's representation, with underlined reserved words and the operator symbols (harness README, 2.1), the message loop and observe block of the harness README example X01 (harnesses/algol-60/README.md, 2.8), and the holding of each relation until its places are known, written for this problem (METRICS.md, rule 19), with no period source;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ CONSTANTS stages 1 and 2 have none. A line 3: k, the integer value of z in the equation z = k of stage 3;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ P01a. Unknowns x, y, z. Stage 1: x = y. Stage 2: y = z. Stage 3: z = k. ALGOL 60 has no unknowns, so each unknown is a Boolean that says whether it has a value and an integer that holds it, and each equation is held as posed until a place is known, when it gives the other place its value or is tested. The only value any stage gives is an integer, so the integer holds every value an unknown can take here;
  i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ n, cap, m, i, code, k, c3, xv, yv, zv, held, pass;
  b̲o̲o̲l̲e̲a̲n̲ xk, yk, zk, r1, r2, r3, changed, inconsistent;

  p̲r̲o̲c̲e̲d̲u̲r̲e̲ equation(ak, av, bk, bv, r);
    b̲o̲o̲l̲e̲a̲n̲ ak, bk, r; i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ av, bv;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ the evaluator of an equation a = b, between two unknowns given by name: with both places known it is tested, with one known it gives the other its value, and with neither it waits. r is the equation, true while it is held;
  b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
    i̲f̲ ak ∧ bk t̲h̲e̲n̲
    b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ i̲f̲ av ≠ bv t̲h̲e̲n̲ inconsistent := t̲r̲u̲e̲; r := f̲a̲l̲s̲e̲ e̲n̲d̲
    e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ ak t̲h̲e̲n̲
    b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ bv := av; bk := t̲r̲u̲e̲; r := f̲a̲l̲s̲e̲; changed := t̲r̲u̲e̲ e̲n̲d̲
    e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ bk t̲h̲e̲n̲
    b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ av := bv; ak := t̲r̲u̲e̲; r := f̲a̲l̲s̲e̲; changed := t̲r̲u̲e̲ e̲n̲d̲
  e̲n̲d̲ equation;

  p̲r̲o̲c̲e̲d̲u̲r̲e̲ value3;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ the evaluator of the equation z = k of stage 3: z is tested if known, else given k;
  b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
    i̲f̲ zk t̲h̲e̲n̲
    b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ i̲f̲ zv ≠ c3 t̲h̲e̲n̲ inconsistent := t̲r̲u̲e̲ e̲n̲d̲
    e̲l̲s̲e̲
    b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ zv := c3; zk := t̲r̲u̲e̲; changed := t̲r̲u̲e̲ e̲n̲d̲;
    r3 := f̲a̲l̲s̲e̲
  e̲n̲d̲ value3;

  p̲r̲o̲c̲e̲d̲u̲r̲e̲ propagate;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ every held equation is examined, in the order posed, again and again until a whole pass gives no unknown a value;
  b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
    changed := t̲r̲u̲e̲;
    f̲o̲r̲ pass := 1 w̲h̲i̲l̲e̲ changed d̲o̲
    b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
      changed := f̲a̲l̲s̲e̲;
      i̲f̲ r1 t̲h̲e̲n̲ equation(xk, xv, yk, yv, r1);
      i̲f̲ r2 t̲h̲e̲n̲ equation(yk, yv, zk, zv, r2);
      i̲f̲ r3 t̲h̲e̲n̲ value3
    e̲n̲d̲
  e̲n̲d̲ propagate;

  p̲r̲o̲c̲e̲d̲u̲r̲e̲ uname(u);
    v̲a̲l̲u̲e̲ u; i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ u;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ output adapter: the name of unknown u, 1 for x, 2 for y, 3 for z;
  i̲f̲ u = 1 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`x') e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ u = 2 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`y') e̲l̲s̲e̲ PRINTTEXT(`z');

  p̲r̲o̲c̲e̲d̲u̲r̲e̲ place(known, v, u);
    v̲a̲l̲u̲e̲ known, v, u; b̲o̲o̲l̲e̲a̲n̲ known; i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ v, u;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ output adapter: a place of an equation, its value if known, else the name of its unknown;
  i̲f̲ known t̲h̲e̲n̲ print(v) e̲l̲s̲e̲ uname(u);

  p̲r̲o̲c̲e̲d̲u̲r̲e̲ state(known, v, inheld, u);
    v̲a̲l̲u̲e̲ known, v, inheld, u; b̲o̲o̲l̲e̲a̲n̲ known, inheld; i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ v, u;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ output adapter: an unknown, as its value, or held by an equation, or free;
  b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
    uname(u);
    i̲f̲ known t̲h̲e̲n̲ b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(` = '); print(v) e̲n̲d̲
    e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ inheld t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(` held')
    e̲l̲s̲e̲ PRINTTEXT(` free')
  e̲n̲d̲ state;

  p̲r̲o̲c̲e̲d̲u̲r̲e̲ relations;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ output adapter: the equations held, separated by commas;
  b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
    i̲f̲ r1 t̲h̲e̲n̲ b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ place(xk, xv, 1); PRINTTEXT(` = '); place(yk, yv, 2) e̲n̲d̲;
    i̲f̲ r1 ∧ r2 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`, ');
    i̲f̲ r2 t̲h̲e̲n̲ b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ place(yk, yv, 2); PRINTTEXT(` = '); place(zk, zv, 3) e̲n̲d̲
  e̲n̲d̲ relations;

  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ harness words: the instance line;
  n := read; cap := read; m := read;
  f̲o̲r̲ i := 1 s̲t̲e̲p̲ 1 u̲n̲t̲i̲l̲ m d̲o̲ code := read;
  xk := yk := zk := r1 := r2 := r3 := inconsistent := f̲a̲l̲s̲e̲;

  f̲o̲r̲ i := 1 w̲h̲i̲l̲e̲ t̲r̲u̲e̲ d̲o̲
  b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
    c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ harness words: one message, the stage it poses, and then that stage's constants;
    code := read; k := read;
    i̲f̲ k = 1 t̲h̲e̲n̲ r1 := t̲r̲u̲e̲
    e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ k = 2 t̲h̲e̲n̲ r2 := t̲r̲u̲e̲
    e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ k = 3 t̲h̲e̲n̲ b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ c3 := read; r3 := t̲r̲u̲e̲ e̲n̲d̲;

    propagate;

    c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ the answer: every unknown, and the equations still held;
    i̲f̲ ¬inconsistent t̲h̲e̲n̲
    b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
      PRINTTEXT(`[answer]');
      state(xk, xv, r1, 1); PRINTTEXT(`, ');
      state(yk, yv, r1 ∨ r2, 2); PRINTTEXT(`, ');
      state(zk, zv, r2 ∨ r3, 3);
      i̲f̲ r1 ∨ r2 t̲h̲e̲n̲ b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`, where '); relations e̲n̲d̲;
      PRINTTEXT(`[/answer]'); NLCR
    e̲n̲d̲;

    c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ observe: the equations held, the values known, and how many equations wait;
    held := (i̲f̲ r1 t̲h̲e̲n̲ 1 e̲l̲s̲e̲ 0) + (i̲f̲ r2 t̲h̲e̲n̲ 1 e̲l̲s̲e̲ 0) + (i̲f̲ r3 t̲h̲e̲n̲ 1 e̲l̲s̲e̲ 0);
    PRINTTEXT(`[observe]');
    i̲f̲ inconsistent t̲h̲e̲n̲ b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`no solution'); NLCR e̲n̲d̲;
    PRINTTEXT(`held equations: ');
    i̲f̲ held = 0 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`none') e̲l̲s̲e̲ relations;
    NLCR;
    i̲f̲ xk t̲h̲e̲n̲ b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`[bind x]'); print(xv); PRINTTEXT(`[/bind]'); NLCR e̲n̲d̲;
    i̲f̲ yk t̲h̲e̲n̲ b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`[bind y]'); print(yv); PRINTTEXT(`[/bind]'); NLCR e̲n̲d̲;
    i̲f̲ zk t̲h̲e̲n̲ b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`[bind z]'); print(zv); PRINTTEXT(`[/bind]'); NLCR e̲n̲d̲;
    i̲f̲ held > 0 t̲h̲e̲n̲
    b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`[suspended held-relations '); print(held); PRINTTEXT(`]'); NLCR e̲n̲d̲;
    PRINTTEXT(`[/observe]'); NLCR; PRINTTEXT(`[end]')
  e̲n̲d̲
e̲n̲d̲
